    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.49) and **Drake Baldwin** (68.73) anchor the Austin Waves lineup as our premier starts. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Fisher, where the combination of a park factor boost and a significant dynamic platoon advantage (14%) elevates his ceiling. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** is in an ideal spot batting second against Rodriguez; his high efficiency is driven by a porous opposing xERA of 4.71 and a strong recent performance trend. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** (62.70) remains a core play; batting leadoff provides the volume necessary to hunt for stolen bases, a vital component for our 5x5 Roto strategy, and he faces a manageable matchup against Melton.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler**, who narrowly missed a stronger grade despite his lead-off position. While **Wade Meckler** (54.93) boasts a solid matchup against Dobnak and a high SP skill score, the optimizer favored the higher-upside profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (61.36) and the primary middle infielders. Conversely, we must monitor the risks surrounding **Andy Pages** (49.11) and **Gunnar Henderson** (42.45). **Andy Pages** is tasked with facing Misiorowski, an elite arm with a dangerous 2.03 xERA, though his score is buoyed by favorable wind conditions. **Gunnar Henderson** faces a similar hurdle against Seymour; while he is a must-start in most contexts, the combination of a tough pitcher and a negative platoon split suppresses his efficiency score significantly today.\n\nRegarding our injury report, the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** continues to strain our depth, leaving us reliant on the high-contact approach of players like **Liam Hicks** (48.67) and **Miguel Vargas** (53.13) to bridge the gap. We are carefully monitoring the status of **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** for late-inning substitutions should any of our active starters encounter defensive replacements or inclement weather delays. With stolen bases at a premium, the speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci** will be watched closely, as their ability to exploit opposing pitching deliveries remains the pivot point for our daily scoring.",
